{
  "id": "joel-malachi-chapter-numbering",
  "kind": "versification",
  "description": "Chapters that differ across traditions: the Hebrew text (org) divides Joel into four chapters where English editions have three (English 2:28-32 is Hebrew 3:1-5 and English 3 is Hebrew 4), and Malachi into three where English has four (English 4:1-6 is Hebrew 3:19-24). Rows run from eng to org; set cases map whole spans, including one that crosses the English chapter boundary. Nothing is asserted about the Septuagint here.",
  "license": "CC0 (numbering facts; no copyrighted text)",
  "source": "Chapter and verse counts compared between the WLC (Hebrew) and the KJV/BSB (English) for Joel and Malachi; the eng scheme name follows Paratext usage.",
